<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Radetzky von Radetz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1766–1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Marshal Radetzky, Field Marshal Radetzky, Joseph Radetzky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Radetzky von Radetz was an Austrian field marshal of Bohemian birth who served as chief of staff in the campaigns of 1813–1814 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Commanding in Lombardy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a>, he withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in the revolution of 1848, defeated Piedmont-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> at Custoza in 1848 and Novara in 1849, and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. He governed Lombardy-Venetia until 1857, and Johann Strauss I's Radetzky March honours him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-radetzky-von-radetz.jpg" alt="Joseph Radetzky von Radetz" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Decker · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Field_Marshal_Johann_Josef_Wenzel_Graf_Radetzky_von_Radetz_(by_Georg_Decker)_-_Heeresgeschichtliches_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
